ed contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Law School at Rutgers University-Newark seeks lecturers and coadjutants for the 2026-2027 semesters (Summer 26, Fall 26, Winter 26, Spring 27) to teach in various disciplines. The instructor will present the course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0550 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience JD Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Rutgers University-Newark is a diverse, research-intensive campus located in Newark, NJ. The campus thrives with a supportive culture that helps students achieve their goals and fosters collaboration among employees. Two schools, each with distinctive strengths, have come together to create a law school offering extraordinary learning opportunities and career growth. Rutgers Law School- with locations in Newark and Camden -offers a world-class faculty; a curriculum of exceptional breadth and depth in theory, practice and interdisciplinary studies; a geographic presence that spans one of the nation’s 10 largets legal markets (New Jersey) while also offering immediate access to two of the five largest markets (New York City and Philadelphia); an alimni netowrk with over 20,000 mebers; and a strong tradition of diversity and social impact. As the law school for a top public university, Rutgers Law School is committed to the highest standards of teaching, scholarship, and service to its host communities, the state of New Jersey, and the nation. Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link