ompetitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Rutgers Business School is seeking individuals to assist with non-instructional assignments for its non-credit programs and centers. Successful candidates will provide assistance, guidance, research, and other duties as assigned (e.g., design, recruitment, curriculum development, course design, research, etc.) on a variety of topics, including, but not limited to: accounting, accounting information systems, financial accounting, government accounting, taxation, administrative studies, finance, economics, real estate, marketing, management, management science and information systems, operational management, strategic leadership, supply chain, and much more. Candidates may be responsible for, but not limited to, the following: Conducting research Preparing materials (e.g., presentations, proposals, documents, etc.) as assigned by the hiring manager Generate reports, summaries, and materials for distribution to internal and external entities Developing curriculum, course designs, and course material review Some positions may be grant funded. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 25FA1259 Posting Open Date 12/01/2025 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires an advanced degree and at least one year of instructional/presentational experience, or a combination of education and experience. The degree requirement may be waived if a candidate is considered a subject matter expert in their field. A doctoral degree is preferred. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment May be required to travel between Rutgers-Newark and Rutgers-New Brunswick campuses. Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265492 Campus Rutgers University-Newark Home Location Campus Rutgers University-Newark City Newark, New Brunswick, and off-campus sites. State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination 